course: dictionary
lesson: 4957
title: Born with it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things you learn, like spelling or riding a bike. Other things you are born with, and nobody has to teach you. An inborn thing is present from birth. The prefix in- means "in", and born means "born", so the word fits its meaning.
explain: «Young cuckoos are raised by other birds and fly to Africa alone, so the route must be inborn.» The young cuckoo never sees a grown cuckoo, so nobody can teach it the way. The clue is the word so: the route is not learned, so it must be inborn.
explain: «Monarch butterflies fly to the same mountain forests in Mexico, and no single butterfly makes the whole round trip, so the route must be inborn.» Look at the reason. No butterfly makes the whole journey, so none of them could have learned the full route from start to finish.
fact: Inborn means present in a person or animal from birth, not learned later.
fact: Examples of inborn things are an inborn talent, an inborn ability and an inborn instinct.
fact: In medicine, an inborn condition is one a baby is born with.
fact: Inborn is the opposite of learned: a learned skill grows with practice.
fact: Young cuckoos fly to Africa alone, so their route is inborn.
exercise: «He has an inborn talent for drawing.» What does inborn mean here? | Learned at school from a good teacher | Very expensive | Hidden under the ground | *Present from birth, not learned later
exercise: Which of these is an inborn ability? | Reading a book in English | *Knowing how to breathe | Playing the piano well after lessons | Riding a bike after weeks of practice
exercise: Why does the text say the monarch butterfly's route must be inborn? | The butterflies only fly at night | The butterflies read maps in the mountains | The mountains are very close to each other | *No single butterfly makes the whole trip, so none could have learned the full route
test: What does an inborn condition mean in medicine? | A condition a doctor cures in one day | A condition caught from a dirty cup | *A condition a baby is born with | A condition only grown-ups can get
test: Which word is the opposite of inborn? | *Learned | Ancient | Barely | Glum
exam: Jayden says the cuckoo's route is inborn. Which clue in the sentence supports him? | Cuckoos are raised by other birds | *The young cuckoo flies to Africa alone, with no grown bird to show it the way | Cuckoos sometimes cross the Sahara | Cuckoos are a kind of bird
